## APIs and independent gate

`run(releasepath, expectedsha)` and CLI `--release ABSOLUTE --sha SHA256` remain unavailable until adjacent Gate276.json supplies exact `CODE` and `tests` receipt bindings. Each receipt must have `passed:true`, kind CODE or tests, a distinct nonempty actor other than publisher276, and `subject` exactly the object from candidate_subject(): filename -> SHA256 for guarded_publisher276.py, release-plan.schema.json and this document. This avoids self-referential hashing: receipt hashes are in the separate gate, candidate hashes in those receipts. Root coordination supplies actual inspected independent receipt bindings after review; an operator must never fabricate receipt fields or PASS. A hash-valid receipt does not authenticate a human identity by itself. No Gate276.json is included in this private candidate.

`run_test_only(releasepath, expectedsha, after_write)` is the sole native fixture entry. Repository, log and release must all be within private_root/Publisher tests/Tests, with guarded ancestors. Production bindings cannot be substituted through run/CLI. Fault callback is permitted only in this explicit API, never in production. Pure helpers and validators do not provide write authority. This candidate author executes no real R or real lease operation. Independent tests own their separate directory and perform only native private fixtures.

## Closed release schema and serial grant

The closed adjacent Draft202012 schema preserves the old plan mechanical fields. `format` is guarded-publication276-v1; root_grant is replaced by `serial_grant` with exact nonce, lease_path, log_root, ordered targets, temporaries, ordered pages and manifest binding. The operator may create this serial grant under authenticated standing276 authority after one-time independent qualification; it is never represented as another Root per-batch permission. `manifest`, `stable_global_lease`, `dual_consumers`, `required_parents` are additional plan fields. `delegation` names exact task276. The separately bound qualification JSON remains exact `{format:'mechanical-qualification276-v1',nonce,authority,policy,delegation,pages:[{page,qualification},...]}`.

Every accessed binding is exact `{path,sha256}`; all original JSON parsing duplicate/nonfinite protections persist. Pages remain1..20, writes1..250. Targets, absolute paths, legal roles, same-parent exclusive temporaries (suffix .publisher276-NONCE.tmp), case collision checks, single-link regular files and every reparse/symlink ancestor check are preserved. Canonical JSON/TXT relative paths must match; existing canonical preimage must be V3, never installed V4. Archives/reviews/publication records are create-only. Canonical/model/raw/TXT, original converter review, existing canonical external review and original approvals/history remain archived and/or preserved as the old complete model/review bytes. Source status changes may alter only exact published JSON/TXT hashes; reversing them must recover all original rows and fields. Work/source/schema/code/consumer/Git/remote writes have no permitted purpose.

## Exact manifest normalizer

`normalize_record(record)` returns source and canonical_preimage copied from their exact same-name fields. All12 actual selection_kind variants share those fields. Root_source_selection has exactly2 observed forms:299 records are an exact path/sha256 binding, returned as source_selection;329 records have exactly baseline binding plus nonempty method string, whose baseline binding is returned as source_selection. The complete original baseline/method selection object remains unchanged in manifest_record provenance. Any other selection shape or blank method rejects; no source/tool content is inferred from historical fields. In628 records,366 have model/text and262 have model/text/raw. Missing raw stays absent in selected source; no native raw is inferred. An actual process may additionally preserve a deterministic restored_raw binding, whose bytes are verified and archived as restored provenance. It is never silently adopted as an authoritative native source. Complete actual original process capture and complete frozen record are retained.

`required_issue_reports(record)` conservatively finds every exact nested binding under key paths containing report, hold or review. All must occur in retained_issue_reports and authenticate. Additional known issue evidence can be retained too. Complete frozen record in final provenance preserves historical_source_hold, source_selection_hold and all contradictory, withdrawn, opaque/unprinted/null/physical/source history even when report formats differ. Known issue text is an operator summary, not a machine adjudication of source semantics; it must be nonempty when required report/hold history exists. The original reports and original review remain complete, so summaries cannot replace them.

## Honest per-page mechanical qualification

Old independent_SOURCE, independent_DATA, reviewers, no-known-loss assertions and old SOURCE/DATA checks are absent and prohibited by the closed schema. Qualification contains source_key, source_selection, tools object converter/renderer/schema, format_decisions, dual_consumers, exact subject, execution, process, conversion_report, emitted_data, retained_issue_reports, known_issues and fixed mechanical checks. `subject` copies the page's source,data,txt,original_review,final_review,schema and qualification's source_key,source_selection,tools,format_decisions,dual_consumers. Bound page schema must equal manifest schema. Source and canonical preimages equal the frozen manifest record exactly. No silent source or tool rebase exists.

`execution` is an operator normalization of observed existing or fresh execution, not a fake converter output. Its exact JSON is `{format:'successful-conversion276-v1',page,exit_code:0,emitted:true,source:PAGE.source,data:QUALIFICATION.emitted_data,txt:PAGE.txt,original_review:PAGE.original_review,tools:QUALIFICATION.tools,format_decisions:QUALIFICATION.format_decisions,process:QUALIFICATION.process,conversion_report:QUALIFICATION.conversion_report}`. All bindings are rehashed. `process` is the actual captured JSON with integer exit_code0, source bindings model/text and optional raw/restored_raw, tools converter/renderer/schema, argv, optional stdout/stderr as either exact captured raw strings (Root244/249/261/271) or exact path/sha256 bindings (new276 executions). Captured strings remain authenticated inside the complete original process bytes and are archived with that process; bindings are additionally rehashed. Other captured-log shapes reject. Actual source and tool hashes must match the selected frozen content. Copied executable/source paths are allowed only when their bytes authenticate, with original paths retained in the actual capture. All actual process source/raw bytes and actual process/report are archived. A normalization alone is insufficient if the process says nonzero exit, changed input/tool or if emitted files/report do not match.

Supported exact converter argv tail after its one converter path is model_path, --text, text_path, --render, --output, emitted_data_parent, --report, conversion_report_path. Different invocation forms are precise unsupported holds until separately reviewed. The report must state dry run false, source writes0, blocked count0, one exact page with status converted or converted with findings, selected source path and exact emitted_data output path. A blocked/nonemitting/nonzero process is a hold; historical converted status alone never qualifies. The independent stage must establish actual reuse provenance from its original execution capture; no new conversion is implied by reuse.

`emitted_data` is original saved V4 before publication metadata changes. Its complete original bytes are archived and its bound schema validated. Final DATA must be exactly equal outside top-level review; original and final content digests exclude only review and must match both converter and final external review digests. Schema, page identity, review/details, inherited review and history checks remain mechanical. Review_delta now permits only an existing reviewer string attribution edit; uncertainty detail, warning and finding edits are forbidden. Adding staged publication provenance and inverting the attribution must recover the full original converter review. No findings collection is removed or rewritten.

Every276 page remains approved false and unresolved discrepancies true, representing its explicitly unreviewed standing-authority publication. Provenance includes old canonical review, selected source review, approved:false, source_approval:false, local_only:true, contract:'successful-current-conversion276-unreviewed', full manifest_record, exact known_issues and retained_issue_reports, unreviewed:true, SOURCE_DATA_PASS:false, no_known_loss_claim:false. Unresolved true is conservative and does not fabricate a specific converter finding. Known typed loss is retained as unreviewed; no wiring approval or source uncertainty resolution is asserted. No new ALD schema fields are added; these are external review/provenance fields under the existing review model.

## Parent creation, complete maps and durable transaction

The exact stable global lease257 is used by every real serial chunk and all cooperating writers including Root. No stale/foreign lock breaking or blind retries occur. The runner exclusively fsyncs nonce.intent.json outside R before any R mkdir, temporary or target write. `required_parents` must equal the sorted depth-then-casefold list of all and only currently missing target ancestors for new archive/review targets under allowed roots. Creation is serialized under the sole lease, guarded immediately before mkdir. Exact parent names are recorded in intent and receipt. Complete subject/schema/binding validation occurs before lease acquisition, allowing only exactly declared missing target parents. Invalid page subjects therefore reject without holding the global lease or blocking other finite pages. No complete R map is observed by the runner until those parents exist. The caller may compute the file-only staged map beforehand; directory creation changes no mapped file. Empty directories intentionally survive failures for reconciliation; no broad directory deletion occurs. A parent/pre-map failure retains lease and precise intent, forbids automatic replay, and requires explicit reconciliation. No directory transaction atomicity is claimed.

Full repository maps include every file except directories .git/.vs, with no caller exclusion. The protected map must equal the whole before-map excluding exact transaction targets, preserving every untouched canonical/source/review/archive/consumer/schema/code file, installed261, later273 installs and other prior/later commits. Each canonical target additionally requires its exact frozen V3 before hash; installed V4 cannot be replayed. Hash-only status verifies current hashes for just these pages. Maps and bindings are reread under lease.

The frozen250 exclusive temp creation, flush/fsync, atomic Windows replace, new-target no-replace rename, exclusive preimage handle, immediate identity/content recheck, exact full after-map, guarded own-byte rollback, foreign-byte preservation, immutable exclusive receipt, archive no-overwrite, postcommit failure and reconciliation logic are retained. Lease remains on any reconciliation; no automatic crash recovery or replay. Receipt failure can leave durable intent+lease as recovery evidence. Atomicity is per file under cooperative serialization; hostile uncooperative writers or ancestor rename races and power-loss multi-file atomicity are not solved. Root and legitimate publishers must honor stable lease. Readonly receipts are exclusive protocol artifacts, not administrator-proof storage.

Receipts report exact release/intent/qualifications, parent intent, success, actual installed pagecount, afterimage observations, complete maps, protected/archive verification, failure, rollback, remainder and reconciliation. The later stage retains immutable exact completed/failed/skipped/remainder finite partitions and advances serially after durable receipts. This publisher executes one exact plan per invocation and never refills, runs conversion, updates Root counters, redispatches twenty273 or installs any shared code. Failed pages can be separately held while other exact finite pages progress.


## Independent CODE findings incorporated in revision008

The exact dual-consumer receipt must have passed true and installed_files containing exactly19 distinct absolute guarded path/sha256 bindings. These actual files are read and rehashed before lease acquisition, again under the lease before writes, and after all writes before commit credit. The inventory includes7 ald_editor files outside R; R maps alone do not protect those. A changed/missing/external consumer is never repaired by this writer. Postwrite failure rolls back only own targets, retains external observations in consumer_verification and reconciliation and preserves the lease. Consumer receipt drift itself also fails closed.

protected_history_verified requires an actual complete before-map, a readable actual after-map, matching untouched R hashes and verified actual19 consumers. A pre-map failure reports false and protected_history_status unavailable-before-complete-map, never vacuous all(empty) success. Consumers are observed again for receipt evidence even on failure.

pagecount and credited_successful_batch_pagecount both credit only an entirely verified successful batch. pagecount_semantics explicitly states that failure count0 is not proof that zero pages were installed. actual_installation_state is fully verified committed batch only on success; otherwise it says actual partial installation remains possible and directs reconciliation to actual_afterimages and complete maps. External drift, failed rollback and postcommit receipt/chmod/lease/stdout failure are never reasons to retry. Durable intent/nonreplay is retained; inspect the intent, maps, archived and canonical observations and receipt availability. A missing completion receipt does not prove zero installation.


## Exact007 CODE HOLD corrections in revision008

A false or unavailable final observe_consumers result after primary successful transaction verification now explicitly sets POSTCOMMIT-UNCREDITED failure before receipt construction. success is false, both batch credit counts are0, commit_credit_status is POSTCOMMIT-UNCREDITED, external consumer observations and reconciliation are retained, and the lease remains. This postcommit classification never claims rollback happened and never claims zero actual installations: writes may already be installed, with actual afterimage observations and full maps retained. No retry is allowed. The changed-window control injects only after primary consumer validation, not via the earlier per-write callback.

On pre-map failure, the final live file map remains recovery evidence. With no complete before-map, the runner reports newness unknown and makes no assertion that any observed existing file is new. Only a known complete before-map can support individual new-path-remains classifications. Protected history remains false/unavailable before a complete map, and no zero-installation inference follows from the uncredited batch count.


